Generate an EPAM-branded PowerPoint deck (.pptx, no PDF) summarizing the code review of ABAP program ZDMS_UPLOAD_FILES carried out on a real SAP system.

Audience: SAP architects + engineering managers, technical-but-not-deep.

Source markdowns (full content in `../`, in this review arc order):
- ../01-target.md — Review target description (ZDMS_UPLOAD_FILES)
- ../02-security.md — Security findings
- ../03-performance.md — Performance findings
- ../04-cleancore.md — Clean Core / S/4 readiness findings
- ../05-maintainability.md — Maintainability findings
- ../06-summary.md — Cross-cutting summary, prioritization
- ../RETRO.md — Retrospective on the review run

Deck must:
- Open with cover (title, subtitle "Code review", date) — EPAM-branded
- Have a contents slide
- One section per review axis: Target → Security → Performance → Clean Core → Maintainability → Summary → Retro
- For each finding category, show severity counts via a BlockGrid (Critical / High / Medium / Low) and list ALL findings (not just one per category) — short titles + 1-line description
- Use HERO_METRIC_TO_THE_LEFT or HERO_METRIC_ON_TOP blocks where a number tells the story
- Keep slide bodies short — favor blocks and short bullets over walls of text
- Finish with priorities / next-steps slide

Final pptx output: ../report.simple-deck.pptx (NOT overwriting the existing report.pptx).

Generate via the simple-deck Python library; run the resulting `presentation.py` with `simple-deck-python`.
